# ─── build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All regenerable. The ESP-IDF trees were tracked once (~4400 files, 7 copies of
# a 5.8 MB compile_commands.json) and are most of why .git is 123 MB for a 16 MB
# working tree. That history also made the first push to GitHub time out.
c/bin/
build/
*/build/
**/build/
sdkconfig.old
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.map
*.d
*.su
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# ─── fetched data, never vendored ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make fetch` downloads the corpora; data/SHA256 is tracked so any run is
# reproducible and any copy is verifiable. The files themselves are 9.8 MB and
# belong to their upstreams, not to this repository.
data/*.json
data/*.csv
data/*.gz
data/*.tsv

# ─── archive: never deleted, never tracked ───────────────────────────────────
# Superseded work, a second git repository, and a Python virtualenv — ~880 MB
# read perhaps once. Inventory and restore steps: doc/ARCHIVE.md
# The one exception is provenance/, which IS tracked: it holds the only off-disk
# copy of three commits that were never pushed anywhere.
archive/

# ─── python era, archived ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# ─── editor / OS cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db

# ─── scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
core

# ESP-IDF regenerates this from sdkconfig.defaults. Tracking it lets the two
# drift — the tracked copy once held CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_QIO=y alongside
# CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE="dio", which cost an hour to understand.
esp32_router/sdkconfig

# Superseded blobs live in archive/superseded_blobs/, not next to the source.
# c/router.bin was a tracked 830 KB d=512 blob from the first C commit that
# nothing referenced. The only tracked blob is the shipped one.
c/*.bin

# WiFi credentials for the wifiprobe measurement build. NEVER commit these.
# Copy esp32_router/main/wifi_creds.h.example and fill it in locally.
esp32_router/main/wifi_creds.h

# Single-file flashable images, produced by `make image`. Build artefacts: they
# are attached to releases by CI, never tracked. Keeping them out also keeps the
# "only tracked .bin is the shipped blob" invariant true.
dist/
